///*!
\page DeviceOmmo Ommo tracking system

Ommo devices provide tracking via an Ommo SIU (Sensor Interface Unit) and a gRPC-based SDK/service.
Plus connects to the Ommo service, discovers connected devices dynamically, and creates tools in the output channel as ports come online.

\section OmmoSupportedHwDevices Supported hardware devices
- Ommo basestation
- Ommo SIU and compatible Ommo IMU sensors
- Each physical SIU port corresponds to one Ommo "device" in Plus
- Multi-sensor devices are exposed as separate tools (one per sensor) on the same port

/// Ommo support in Plus
\section OmmoSupportedPlatforms Supported platforms

- Windows 64-bit (Plus built with Ommo support; Ommo gRPC service reachable)
- Linux 64-bit (Plus built with Ommo support; Ommo gRPC service reachable)

Note: The Ommo SDK and client libraries are built as part of the Plus superbuild.
On the Plus side you only need the Ommo gRPC service (`ommo_service`) running and
reachable at the configured GrpcAddress.

\section OmmoInstallation Installation

- Install the Ommo SDK / runtime and Ommo gRPC service according to vendor instructions.
- Ensure the Ommo gRPC service is running and reachable on the configured \c GrpcAddress
  (typically \c "localhost:50051" on the same machine as PlusServer).

\section OmmoCoordinateSystems Coordinate systems

Ommo SDK reports poses in its own tracker coordinate system; Plus exposes them as transforms
to the \c ToolReferenceFrame (usually \c "Tracker"):

- \c Ommo_<UUID>_P<port>ToTracker:    Single-sensor device on SIU UUID \c <UUID>, port \c <port>
- \c Ommo_<UUID>_P<port>_S<sensor>ToTracker: Multi-sensor device on SIU UUID \c <UUID>,
  port \c <port>, sensor index \c <sensor>

Tool names are kept compact so they fit within the 20-character OpenIGTLink transform name limit
for easy display in 3D Slicer and other clients.

\section OmmoConfigSettings Device configuration settings

- \xmlAtt \ref DeviceType "Type" = \c "Ommo" \RequiredAtt
- \xmlAtt \ref DeviceAcquisitionRate "AcquisitionRate" \OptionalAtt{100}
- \xmlAtt \ref ToolReferenceFrame \OptionalAtt{Tracker}
- \xmlAtt \ref LocalTimeOffsetSec \OptionalAtt{0}

Ommo-specific attributes on the \c Device element:

- \xmlAtt \b GrpcAddress \OptionalAtt{"localhost:50051"}
  - gRPC address of the Ommo service (e.g. \c "localhost:50051" or \c "192.168.1.10:50051").

- \xmlAtt \b RequiredDeviceIds \OptionalAtt{""}
  - Comma-separated list of SIU UUIDs (numeric 32-bit IDs) for devices that must be present.
  - If specified:
    - Only devices whose \c siu_uuid is in this list are accepted; others are ignored.
    - Recording will not start until **all** required devices have connected within
      \c DeviceWaitTimeoutSec.

- \xmlAtt \b DeviceWaitTimeoutSec \OptionalAtt{30.0}
  - Timeout in seconds to wait for all required devices (from \c RequiredDeviceIds) to connect.
  - If the timeout is reached and some required devices are still missing, Plus reports an error
    and does not start recording.

- \xmlAtt \b ConnectionDelaySec \OptionalAtt{2.0}
  - Used when \c RequiredDeviceIds is **not** specified.
  - Delay in seconds after the Ommo channel becomes ready before starting device discovery
    and recording (allows devices to connect after startup).

- \xmlAtt \b BaseStationStartupDelaySec \OptionalAtt{10.0}
  - Delay in seconds to wait for the SIU/base station motor spin-up before starting acquisition.
  - Increase this value if the base station needs more time to report stable tracking.

- \xmlAtt \b PositionScaleFactor \OptionalAtt{1.0}
  - Scale factor applied to Ommo position values so Plus outputs millimeters.
  - Typical values:
    - \c 1.0  : Ommo SDK already reports in mm.
    - \c 10.0 : Ommo SDK reports in cm (cm * 10 = mm).
    - \c 1000.0 : Ommo SDK reports in meters (m * 1000 = mm).

- \xmlAtt \b BadDataThreshold \OptionalAtt{0.5}
  - Threshold in \[0.0, 1.0\] for the Ommo \c bad_data_indicator.
  - If the indicator exceeds this threshold, the tool status is marked as out-of-view.
  - Increase the threshold to be more tolerant of marginal tracking quality.

Channel configuration:

- \xmlElem \ref OutputChannels One \c OutputChannel used for all Ommo tools. \RequiredAtt
  - \xmlElem \ref OutputChannel \RequiredAtt
    - \xmlAtt \ref Id \RequiredAtt
      - All dynamically created Ommo tools are added to this channel.

\section OmmoDeviceDiscovery Device discovery and tool creation

- Tools are created dynamically when Ommo devices connect to the SIU.
- Each SIU UUID + port ID pair corresponds to one device in Plus:
  - Single-sensor: one tool per port.
  - Multi-sensor: one tool per sensor on the same port.
- If \c RequiredDeviceIds is specified, only devices whose numeric SIU UUID (\c siu_uuid)
  appears in that list will be accepted; other devices are ignored.

\section OmmoExampleConfigFile Example configuration files

Example Ommo PlusServer configuration (server + recording):

- \include "ConfigFiles/PlusDeviceSet_Server_Ommo.xml"

Example Ommo data-collection-only configuration:

- \include "ConfigFiles/Testing/PlusDeviceSet_DataCollectionOnly_Ommo.xml"

*/